def elevator_sweep_stops(start_floor, direction, requests, top_floor):
    visited = set(requests)
    if direction == 1:
        stop = start_floor
        while stop <= top_floor:
            if stop in visited:
                yield stop
            stop += 1
        if top_floor in visited and stop - 1 != top_floor:
            yield top_floor
    else:
        stop = start_floor
        while stop >= 1:
            if stop in visited:
                yield stop
            stop -= 1
        if 1 in visited and stop + 1 != 1:
            yield 1
    return list(visitor)
```

At every floor the elevator stops to check whether it is a requested floor, and if so records it. When going up the stopping range is from the start floor to the top floor and includes both endpoints; when going down it is from the start floor to floor 1 and also includes both endpoints. Because the requested floors are stored as a set, order is not preserved, so yields must be used. The final floor in each direction is double-checked separately; if it is requested and the outer loop already passed it, the visiting yield catches it. The values are then gathered into a list and returned in the order the elevator encounters them.

