The function keeps a list of the people in the order they arrived and handles events in the given sequence. When an arrive event comes in, the person is appended to the list. When a serve event is encountered, the first up to capacity names are popped from the front and kept, and the list is then replaced by those names. When the queue is shorter than the capacity, only its remaining names are kept and the list is not cleared. A deque is used temporarily so that popping from the front happens quickly.

